WEBVTT

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:34.650
Next, Hiyori Corp, a rapidly growing
software company, has folded.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.010
Other companies connected to Hiyori,

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:41.040
including Risan Electronics,
Karui Company and Katsugi Inc.,

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.560
have also gone bankrupt
in a chain reaction.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.180
This concludes today's news.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:52.560
Yagami!

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.470
Good morning!

00:01:56.070 --> 00:02:00.930
Poor Godai.
Just when he got a job...

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.900
Huh? Did something
happen to Godai?

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.870
What? You haven't heard?

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:08.400
About what?

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:10.180
This.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:13.960
Oh!

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:18.720
Isn't Katsugi Inc. the company
that your dad introduced him to?

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:24.870
Maybe he's lying in bed
from shock.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.800
What if he hung himself?

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:29.000
Poor Godai.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:33.870
- Oh, no! We're going to be late!
- Wait!

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.310
Yagami! You're going to be tardy.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:15.050
Did something happen?
Ms. Otonashi looks depressed.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.750
- It's probably about Godai.
- Godai?

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:23.430
Did something happen to him?

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:24.720
Actually...

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:30.970
What?

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:35.220
I see...
So his job fell through.

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:40.080
I have to say
he's hard on luck, that Godai...

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:41.400
Shun!

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:50.780
What is it, Uncle?

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.690
Pay a visit to Asuna tomorrow.

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:54.690
What?!

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:56.620
Who's Asuna?

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:00.430
She's the woman that the coach
had a marriage meeting with.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.340
Did something happen
to Asuna?

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:12.630
I'm not sure but she doesn't
want to get out of bed.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:15.300
Go check on her and
earn some points.

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:19.640
Give it a rest, Uncle.
I have someone else that I love.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.050
You're so persistent.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:25.220
Why haven't you brought her around?
Let me meet her.

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:27.650
What's up your sleeve?

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:29.410
She's right here.

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:30.910
Ms. Ichinose!

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.220
I see...

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.210
So that's your taste
in women?

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:45.360
What do you mean by that?

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:49.940
The type that looks like a
beer keg wearing clothes?

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:52.210
Which one are you looking at?

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:55.100
Who's he calling a beer keg
wearing clothing?

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.780
- How witty.
- Yes.

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:00.040
- Grr!
- I mean...

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:07.700
Oh, now I see.
She's quite a beauty.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:09.850
Uncle!

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:15.220
I can see why you like her, but
go and visit Asuna anyway.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:18.640
I already told them you'd
visit tomorrow.

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:21.100
You can't make decisions
like that for me!

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:23.780
See you.
I'll tag along too.

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:24.950
Uncle!

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.590
Wait, Uncle!

00:05:32.090 --> 00:05:34.590
Grr! What a troublemaker.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:38.150
Hey, you. You still got ties to that girl
from the marriage meeting?

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:40.830
I guess I do.

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:44.270
But don't worry,
Ms. Otonashi.

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:51.340
At this next meeting,
I'll end it once and for all.

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:52.970
D-Don't do that.

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:57.020
Why did you tell him
not to do it?

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:01.020
- You don't care?
- Well...

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:05.010
Has there been any progress
with Godai?

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:06.550
What do you mean by that?

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:11.190
It's just that the other girl has
more going for her than I do.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:13.980
I think she's better
for Mr. Mitaka.

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:16.660
How proper.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:19.570
So what happened with Godai?

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:22.340
Why... ! Nothing!

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:31.740
Godai?

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:33.470
M-Manager...

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:34.910
Are you going out?

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:39.820
Yes. I might be late since
I'm going drinking with Sakamoto.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:40.650
Bye.

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:47.110
Don't be too down.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:51.330
That's right. There are tons
of other companies out there.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:57.160
P-Please.
I'm not down at all.

00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:59.600
It wasn't that big a deal.
See you.

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:08.610
He acts strong,
but he's crying inside.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:13.040
After all, it's like being dropped
down from heaven into hell.

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:15.190
I don't blame him.

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:31.660
What? Why the angry face?

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:36.910
Why did you introduce Godai
to a company that was about to fold?

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:39.010
Oh, it's about that.

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:42.040
I never dreamed that would happen.

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:44.040
Take responsibility.

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:46.970
Responsibility? How?

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:49.350
Introduce him to another company.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:50.920
Another company?

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:55.260
Of course! Otherwise
I feel sorry for Godai.

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:58.220
I can't face him either.

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:03.200
No. I've done all that
I can already.

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:05.340
Hey, Mom, draw my bath.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:06.210
Dad!

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:32.170
Hello?
Oh, Uncle.

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:37.130
Hi, Shun. I have somewhere
to stop by tomorrow,

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:39.810
so you go ahead to
the Kujo house.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:40.630
Okay.

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:44.570
Oh, well.

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:49.250
It'll be easier to talk
without Uncle there anyway.

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:56.660
Bye. See you later, McEnroe.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:08.210
Since I've gotten over
my phobia of dogs,

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:10.940
I no longer fear the dog maiden.

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:22.350
What? You haven't told Asuna
that Mr. Mitaka is coming?

00:09:22.750 --> 00:09:27.690
No. I don't feel right about
her marrying him.

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:30.110
Is it because of his dealings
with women?

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:39.070
No. Every time Mr. Mitaka
comes over, he looks so wan.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.470
I don't think he's healthy.

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:45.230
I haven't heard otherwise.

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:48.070
I don't think he should
see Asuna.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.740
We can't do that.

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:56.840
Asuna has been depressed
since Mitaka hasn't called.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:02.380
Maybe he's just lovesick.

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:03.920
I doubt it.

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:18.700
Mr. Mitaka...

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:43.830
Hello.

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:46.730
Why, you're Mr. Mitaka's uncle.

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:49.260
Sorry to drop in unexpectedly.

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:52.680
What? Mr. Mitaka's uncle?

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:02.550
Er...what did you want
to talk about?

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:05.380
I'll get right to the point.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:09.250
I beg of you!
Please break it off with Shun!

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:13.020
Please! Please!

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:16.300
I'll compensate you for
calling it off.

00:11:16.470 --> 00:11:18.470
Er...there's nothing
to break off.

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:21.630
J-Just a minute!
You're being rude!

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:23.020
Godai!

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:27.580
So how much are you
willing to shell out?

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:29.140
- Ms. Ichinose!
- Ms. Ichinose!

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:33.110
Er, Mr. Mitaka and I don't
have any special relationship.

00:11:33.190 --> 00:11:35.550
But he proposed to you.

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:40.330
W-Well, yes...but nothing
more has happened since then.

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:42.640
You weren't planning
on saying yes, were you?

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:45.260
I see.

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:49.570
So it was one-sided on Shun's part?
I'm so glad!

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:52.470
Hey! Don't hold her hand
like that!

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:54.720
I'm sorry.
That was rude of me.

00:11:54.810 --> 00:12:02.000
I'm so relieved. It's a happy ending
for all then.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.460
Kyoko has such high standards.

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:27.810
Even a guy like Mr. Mitaka
isn't good enough.

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:29.350
Godai...

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:33.370
It's not going to be easy,
but hang in there.

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:42.480
Godai...

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:45.640
The head of the preschool!

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:47.420
Hi.

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:08.840
Do or die!

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:14.260
Hello...

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:16.900
Oh, Mr. Mitaka!

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:23.350
Come and get me!

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:26.370
S-Stroganoff!

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:28.900
Yahh!

00:13:40.940 --> 00:13:42.700
Mr. Mitaka...

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:45.500
H-Hello!

00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:57.050
Ohh...

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:02.820
This...

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:07.230
No, this one.
No...

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:09.880
This one...or this...

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:12.860
Oh!

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:28.850
I'm so sorry, Mr. Mitaka.
Your suit got dirty.

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.860
No, it's okay.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:35.910
Why didn't you get out of the way
of the charging St. Bernard?

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:37.690
Well, I just...

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:43.460
Oh, Asuna!
Are you feeling all right now?

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:48.230
Welcome.

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:50.660
Hello. Long time no see.

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:54.860
Now how should I bring up
the subject of breaking it off?

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:58.310
I hear you're ill.

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:01.850
She hasn't had much energy
these days.

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:05.140
Not at all.
I feel much better.

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:11.110
Er, this is a get-well gift.
You may not need it anymore.

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:12.370
My!

00:15:17.530 --> 00:15:18.430
I'm so happy!

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:22.120
Er...It's nothing to cry over.

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:26.490
I'm sorry. It's just that
I'm so touched right now!

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:30.310
Perhaps it was lovesickness
after all.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:34.190
Yes. The color has returned
to her cheeks all of a sudden.

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:38.500
Oh, man. I didn't think you'd
be so happy over it.

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:41.250
I'm happy. So happy.
So happy. So happy.

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:42.450
So happy...

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:47.610
Oh, aren't you glad Mr. Mitaka
stopped by today?

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:49.010
My pleasure.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:55.100
I guess I won't bring
the subject up today.

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:00.230
What's going on
with the dogs?

00:16:00.550 --> 00:16:02.900
They must be excited because

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:04.710
Mr. Mitaka, whom I love
so much, is here.

00:16:04.850 --> 00:16:10.480
The dogs were dejected because
Asuna hasn't been playing with them.

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:12.590
I see. Well then...

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:17.480
- Shall I exercise them for you?
- Oh, my. We couldn't impose.

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:18.980
It's no problem.

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:21.060
Go!

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:29.260
I can't let them suck me further
in with more conversation.

00:16:30.610 --> 00:16:31.570
Good dog.

00:16:37.610 --> 00:16:39.160
Ready? Fetch!

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:44.350
Mr. Mitaka is so much more energetic
than we've seen him before.

00:16:44.860 --> 00:16:48.370
Perhaps he was overanxious.
It affected his health.

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:53.860
You're right. Look at how healthy he is.
And energetic, too.

00:16:53.940 --> 00:16:57.380
Hello.
I let myself in.

00:16:57.470 --> 00:16:58.450
Mr. Mitaka!

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:01.330
- I have good news.
- Huh?

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:06.810
I stopped by the home of the widow,
whom we've been hearing about.

00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:13.630
She doesn't feel the same way?

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:15.210
No.

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:16.990
Then...

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:19.640
There is no problem.

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:26.150
Good dogs.

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:33.220
Godai, would you consider
coming back to your old job?

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:36.840
We don't have any trainees
anymore since summer vacation is over.

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:39.360
I'm in a bind because
we're shorthanded.

00:17:42.050 --> 00:17:47.540
But I haven't found a permanent job yet.
I may just be a burden.

00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:52.550
Not at all. You can
job hunt all you want.

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:59.620
We'll manage. It's just until we find
another daycare worker, okay?

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:05.090
Besides, the children are all
waiting for you to come back.

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:14.040
Good day.

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:20.610
Godai, are you sure
you want to work?

00:18:20.760 --> 00:18:23.750
It's such a crucial time now.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:27.520
Yes. Besides, I already
promised him.

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:31.610
Yeah. You're the type that
just can't say no.

00:18:32.190 --> 00:18:35.920
So true. That's the mark of
a wishy-washy personality.

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:39.040
But it might be a nice
change of pace.

00:18:39.170 --> 00:18:40.800
You think so?

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:44.150
Sure! Just think of it
as a change of pace.

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:45.700
Y-Yeah.

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:49.360
Here you go, Dad.
To go with your drink.

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:54.700
What's with the puzzled look, Dad?

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:57.810
- You made this?
- That's right.

00:18:57.920 --> 00:18:59.320
Doesn't it look good?

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:02.610
And it tastes good too.
Try it.

00:19:02.770 --> 00:19:03.950
Okay.

00:19:06.100 --> 00:19:07.360
- Wait.
- Huh?

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.390
- Did you find another company?
- Huh?

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:15.900
I have to tell you, Ibuki...

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:20.010
Dad, are you really planning
to look for another one?

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:22.080
It's not up to me.
I can't...

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:24.400
Then what's going to happen
to Godai?

00:19:24.610 --> 00:19:27.940
What does it matter?
It's no concern of yours.

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:31.860
Dad, you idiot!

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:34.990
H-How dare you call me that!

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:36.610
You are one. That's why
I called you one.

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:39.600
Idiot!  Idiot! Idiot!  Idiot!

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:46.460
- I'm off!
- Bye!

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:50.190
He looks awfully happy.

00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:53.030
It's because he'll get
to see the kids again.

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:55.570
Enough to get over the shock
of the company folding?

00:19:55.940 --> 00:19:58.200
That's Godai's good point.

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:04.470
Look! Look!

00:20:04.860 --> 00:20:05.940
Watch me!

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:12.870
Hey! It's Godai!

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:13.920
Oh!

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:16.720
Hi!

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:18.000
Yay!

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:19.890
- Godai!
- How have you all been?

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:24.190
Settle down. I'll be your playmate
again from today.

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:27.810
Come here.
Upsy daisy!

00:20:28.170 --> 00:20:31.080
Godai will be a big help
now that he's back.

00:20:31.550 --> 00:20:36.170
I know.
And he's so popular with the kids.

00:20:37.030 --> 00:20:39.920
Isn't this fun?
Upsy daisy!

00:20:45.420 --> 00:20:46.820
Hey, Yagami.

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:51.060
What technique are you going to
use to persuade your dad today?

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:53.570
I just can't get through
to him.

00:20:54.010 --> 00:20:56.860
So you're giving up?

00:20:57.470 --> 00:21:00.160
I've made up my mind.

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:02.200
About what?

00:21:04.440 --> 00:21:05.660
- Come here.
- Huh?

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:10.870
What?!

00:21:20.100 --> 00:21:23.000
Playing with kids
is exhausting.

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:36.810
I'm home, Soichiro.

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:44.760
Ya-Yagami.

00:21:52.190 --> 00:21:53.950
Welcome home.

00:21:54.570 --> 00:21:58.460
My father has caused you
much inconvenience.

00:21:59.240 --> 00:22:00.950
W-What's going on?

00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:04.120
- I've left home again.
- What?!

00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:07.300
Until my father finds you
another company

00:22:07.370 --> 00:22:12.310
and you are hired,
I will not move back home.

00:22:12.820 --> 00:22:15.970
I will stay by your side
to take care of you.

00:22:16.650 --> 00:22:23.140
And so, I would like to ask all
of you for your cooperation.

00:22:23.390 --> 00:22:25.220
Same here.

00:22:29.570 --> 00:22:32.830
Come on, Godai.
Dinner is ready.

00:22:32.900 --> 00:22:35.190
Hey! Wait a minute!
Hold on!

00:22:36.110 --> 00:22:38.770
Everyone, excuse us.

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:42.310
Y-Yagami! Wait!
Listen to me.

00:22:42.590 --> 00:22:45.370
She never gives up.

00:22:45.440 --> 00:22:48.200
That's the power of youth.

00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:50.510
What are you going to do, Manager?

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:54.790
What? Well, whatever will be
will be.

00:22:57.500 --> 00:23:00.590
- She's taking this well.
- Yeah.

00:23:06.040 --> 00:23:10.720
Oh, my. That's right.
I worked hard to make it.

00:23:11.010 --> 00:23:13.960
Let's eat before it gets cold.

00:23:14.640 --> 00:23:16.340
Open your mouth, Godai.

00:23:16.590 --> 00:23:19.580
S-Stupid.
What are you doing, Yagami?

00:23:19.650 --> 00:23:22.250
It's okay.
No one is watching.

00:23:23.330 --> 00:23:25.150
I can't see you,
but I can certainly hear you.

00:23:28.500 --> 00:23:30.330
No, don't run away.

00:23:30.500 --> 00:23:32.420
Enough is enough, Yagami!

00:23:33.160 --> 00:23:36.500
Godai, you have rice
stuck on your nose.

00:23:36.610 --> 00:23:40.010
- Let me take it off.
- Cut it out! I'm going to get mad!

00:23:40.170 --> 00:23:41.510
- Say...
- No!

00:23:45.790 --> 00:23:48.020
What? Mitaka turned down
the marriage arrangement?

00:23:48.090 --> 00:23:50.320
And, in front of everyone,
what if he says...

00:23:50.390 --> 00:23:52.960
"Kyoko, will you marry me?"

00:23:53.030 --> 00:23:54.380
That clinches it.

00:23:54.470 --> 00:23:56.420
Damn! I'm not letting him
steal her away from me!

00:23:56.570 --> 00:24:00.320
Next: "I'll Wait!
Kyoko's Double-Duty Declaration"

00:24:00.510 --> 00:24:01.890
K-Kyoko!
